I'm here on a referral
from Professor Mikumo.

53
00:02:55,213 --> 00:02:58,416
I'm scheduled to have an interview
with the manager.

54
00:03:01,319 --> 00:03:02,887
Um… Where's the manager?

55
00:03:03,388 --> 00:03:04,589
That's me.

56
00:03:05,723 --> 00:03:07,392
Oh, I apologize.

57
00:03:07,458 --> 00:03:08,960
I'm Tatsuki Ukita, the manager.

58
00:03:09,027 --> 00:03:11,963
I'm Shizuku Aomine.

59
00:03:12,030 --> 00:03:12,964
Ao…

60
00:03:13,031 --> 00:03:14,065
Aom…

61
00:03:14,599 --> 00:03:16,434
-Aomine…
-Shizuku Aomine.

62
00:03:17,368 --> 00:03:19,537
Please just call me Shizuku.

63
00:03:21,706 --> 00:03:23,541
-Ms. Shizuku.
-Yes.

64
00:03:23,608 --> 00:03:25,076
You were…

65
00:03:25,910 --> 00:03:28,212
You were a teacher
at Musashino Daihachi Middle School?

66
00:03:28,279 --> 00:03:29,414
Yes.

67
00:03:30,014 --> 00:03:32,116
I worked as a teacher
for about five years,

68
00:03:32,617 --> 00:03:34,285
but I left due to personal reasons.

69
00:03:35,653 --> 00:03:36,721
Why this alternative school?

70
00:03:37,288 --> 00:03:40,925
I really want to continue working
with children.

71
00:03:43,594 --> 00:03:44,562
You play video games?

72
00:03:44,629 --> 00:03:46,164
-What?
-Video games.

73
00:03:46,998 --> 00:03:48,966
I've never played them before.

74
00:03:49,534 --> 00:03:51,969
Then what about shogi,
card games, or board games?

75
00:03:53,171 --> 00:03:54,038
Sorry, no.

76
00:03:54,605 --> 00:03:55,707
I see.

77
00:03:57,475 --> 00:03:58,776
Any other special skills?

78
00:03:58,843 --> 00:04:00,545
I can tutor.

79
00:04:00,611 --> 00:04:03,081
For Japanese and English,
I can teach from basics to advanced.

80
00:04:04,182 --> 00:04:05,316
That's not what I meant.

81
00:04:07,552 --> 00:04:09,287
Do you own a hoodie?

82
00:04:09,821 --> 00:04:11,122
-Hoodie?
-Yeah.

83
00:04:12,223 --> 00:04:13,358
Yes, I believe so.

84
00:04:13,424 --> 00:04:14,459
Okay.

85
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:18,162
But you can't play games, huh.

86
00:04:19,697 --> 00:04:20,698
Tatsuki.

87
00:04:21,666 --> 00:04:22,900
They want to go outside.

88
00:04:22,967 --> 00:04:24,369
I want to play color tag.

89
00:04:24,435 --> 00:04:26,003
Good idea.

90
00:04:26,070 --> 00:04:27,238
Let's see…

91
00:04:27,305 --> 00:04:29,073
What should I do?

92
00:04:31,376 --> 00:04:33,811
I'll contact you
with the results at a later date.

93
00:04:33,878 --> 00:04:34,712
Thank you.

94
00:04:36,447 --> 00:04:37,615
Um…

95
00:04:38,416 --> 00:04:39,517
I…

96
00:04:41,386 --> 00:04:43,988
didn't go to school for six years
starting in middle school.

97
00:04:44,489 --> 00:04:47,258
So I think I understand
the feelings of kids

98
00:04:47,325 --> 00:04:48,926
experiencing school refusal.

99
00:04:49,494 --> 00:04:51,429
That's my special skill!

100
00:05:11,115 --> 00:05:11,983
You're hired.

101
00:05:14,986 --> 00:05:16,320
You're hired.

102
00:05:17,288 --> 00:05:18,122
You're hired.

103
00:05:18,189 --> 00:05:19,023
You're hired.

104
00:05:21,926 --> 00:05:24,362
I'm Soya Kaido, a volunteer staff member.

105
00:05:24,429 --> 00:05:25,963
Everyone calls me Soya.

106
00:05:26,531 --> 00:05:27,465
Mr. Soya.

107
00:05:27,532 --> 00:05:29,434
I'm Shizuku Aomine.

108
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:31,469
-Nice to meet you.
-Nice to meet you.

109
00:05:31,536 --> 00:05:33,771
Everyone here calls each other
by nicknames.

110
00:05:33,838 --> 00:05:35,306
What would you like yours to be?

111
00:05:35,373 --> 00:05:36,741
A nickname?

112
00:05:37,308 --> 00:05:38,876
Then…

113
00:05:38,943 --> 00:05:40,211
Please call me Shi-chan.

114
00:05:40,278 --> 00:05:42,413
Very nice!

115
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:43,915
Attention everyone!

116
00:05:44,482 --> 00:05:47,518
This is Shi-chan, who will be joining
as the newest staff member!

117
00:05:47,585 --> 00:05:48,586
-Hello.
-Shi-chan.

118
00:05:48,653 --> 00:05:50,421
-Shi-chan!
-Nice to meet you.

119
00:05:53,791 --> 00:05:54,725
Nice to meet you.

120
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:57,195
Whoa, watch out. Don't cut me.

121
00:05:57,261 --> 00:05:59,363
Basically, everyone here just hangs out

122
00:05:59,430 --> 00:06:01,699
and does whatever they feel like doing.

123
00:06:01,766 --> 00:06:03,734
They can do homework,

124
00:06:03,801 --> 00:06:05,036
play games,

125
00:06:05,102 --> 00:06:07,905
or even just take a nap
like that kid over there.

126
00:06:08,506 --> 00:06:11,509
There are no specific rules here?

127
00:06:12,109 --> 00:06:16,514
Well, they have to put their belongings
in a locker when they get here.

128
00:06:17,281 --> 00:06:19,717
And they have to throw away trash
in the wastebasket.

129
00:06:19,784 --> 00:06:21,219
Throw trash in the wastebasket.

130
00:06:21,285 --> 00:06:22,153
I see.

131
00:06:22,220 --> 00:06:25,957
I know there are various types
of alternative schools,

132
00:06:26,023 --> 00:06:26,924
but what type is this…

133
00:06:27,959 --> 00:06:30,228
This is the safe haven type.

134
00:06:31,562 --> 00:06:33,030
Safe haven type.

135
00:06:35,266 --> 00:06:37,768
This is the kitchen and dining room area.

136
00:06:38,503 --> 00:06:40,071
They're making lunch?

137
00:06:40,137 --> 00:06:42,673
Yeah. Hey guys, what's on the menu today?

138
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:44,909
Curry with fried chicken and salad.

139
00:06:44,976 --> 00:06:46,611
How many layers of the onion do I peel?

140
00:06:46,677 --> 00:06:47,612
I'll do it.

141
00:06:47,678 --> 00:06:49,213
All right.

142
00:06:49,780 --> 00:06:50,982
Hello. I'm Ajiki.

143
00:06:51,048 --> 00:06:52,250
Hello.

144
00:06:52,316 --> 00:06:54,418
I'm Shizuku Aomine.

145
00:06:55,586 --> 00:06:57,021
Call me Shi-chan.

146
00:06:57,088 --> 00:06:58,523
I'm Ajicchan. Nice to meet you.

147
00:06:58,589 --> 00:06:59,957
Nice to meet you.

148
00:07:00,658 --> 00:07:03,528
Everyone cooks together?

149
00:07:03,594 --> 00:07:05,363
Once a week.
And participation is optional.

150
00:07:05,429 --> 00:07:07,298
We all decide on the menu together.

151
00:07:07,365 --> 00:07:08,799
We made gratin last week.

152
00:07:08,866 --> 00:07:10,268
-Oh.
-I see.

153
00:07:10,334 --> 00:07:11,836
Please make the salad.

154
00:07:11,903 --> 00:07:13,170
Just tear up the lettuce.

155
00:07:13,237 --> 00:07:14,505
-Oh, but…
-Thanks.

156
00:07:14,572 --> 00:07:15,973
Just tear it?

157
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:17,575
-Let's see…
-Oh!

158
00:07:17,642 --> 00:07:20,344
Shi-chan, can you show the guests
to the atelier?

159
00:07:20,411 --> 00:07:22,013
-Me?
-Yeah, sorry.

160
00:07:22,813 --> 00:07:24,649
I'm Saotome.

161
00:07:27,618 --> 00:07:28,719
Say hello.

162
00:07:34,425 --> 00:07:35,593
She's Ayaka.

163
00:07:37,061 --> 00:07:38,729
She had been skipping school

164
00:07:38,796 --> 00:07:41,499
on and off during the first year
of middle school,

165
00:07:41,999 --> 00:07:43,801
but ever since she started
the second year,

166
00:07:43,868 --> 00:07:45,703
she's been unable to go to school at all.

167
00:07:46,270 --> 00:07:47,505
I see.

168
00:07:48,205 --> 00:07:51,576
Lately, her days and nights
have gotten completely flipped around,

169
00:07:51,642 --> 00:07:52,843
and her lifestyle is irregular,

170
00:07:53,644 --> 00:07:57,548
so I'm hoping to get her back
to a normal routine.

171
00:08:05,423 --> 00:08:08,125
All this artwork was drawn
by the kids here.

172
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:10,661
Isn't this interesting?

173
00:08:12,830 --> 00:08:15,566
Since she's been refusing
to go to school for so long,

174
00:08:16,067 --> 00:08:18,536
I'm worried that she'll fall behind
on her studies.

175
00:08:22,573 --> 00:08:23,441
That's understandable.

176
00:08:24,008 --> 00:08:28,012
How are the kids here studying…?

177
00:08:28,079 --> 00:08:29,880
They hardly study at all.

178
00:08:31,048 --> 00:08:34,585
They usually play games,
go outside to play, or draw.

179
00:08:35,252 --> 00:08:36,087
I'm sorry.

180
00:08:37,955 --> 00:08:40,925
I'm usually playing games
until late at night,

181
00:08:40,992 --> 00:08:42,560
so I'm sleep-deprived every day.

182
00:08:43,995 --> 00:08:45,429
-I see.
-Yup.

183
00:08:47,064 --> 00:08:48,432
If you want to get her to study,

184
00:08:48,499 --> 00:08:50,968
you'll be better off throwing away
the textbooks altogether.

185
00:08:51,769 --> 00:08:52,737
‎What?

186
00:08:55,373 --> 00:08:58,943
I actually used to work
as a middle school teacher.

187
00:08:59,010 --> 00:09:01,379
So I can help out with the schoolwork.

188
00:09:01,445 --> 00:09:02,680
I see.

189
00:09:03,714 --> 00:09:04,548
Good for you.

190
00:09:06,851 --> 00:09:09,954
Did Ayaka say
that she wanted to come here?

191
00:09:11,756 --> 00:09:13,691
I checked the reviews online,

192
00:09:13,758 --> 00:09:16,027
and when I told her about this place,

193
00:09:16,093 --> 00:09:18,663
she said she wanted to check it out.

194
00:09:19,296 --> 00:09:20,464
I see.

195
00:09:21,465 --> 00:09:25,770
How long do people stay here
for their school refusal to be cured?

196
00:09:25,836 --> 00:09:27,405
It's not something that can be cured.

197
00:09:29,373 --> 00:09:31,475
Not going to school is also a way of life.

198
00:09:35,046 --> 00:09:37,114
But in that case, what about her future…

199
00:09:37,915 --> 00:09:40,718
What matters more is the present,
not the future.

200
00:09:46,524 --> 00:09:48,793
Do you have any other concerns?

201
00:09:50,428 --> 00:09:51,262
No, thank you.

202
00:09:52,029 --> 00:09:52,997
Okay.

203
00:09:54,732 --> 00:09:57,334
While you're here,
only do things that you think are fun.

204
00:10:00,037 --> 00:10:01,272
Want to draw something?

205
00:10:02,273 --> 00:10:03,774
Let's see.

206
00:10:04,275 --> 00:10:06,043
This might be good.

207
00:10:06,110 --> 00:10:08,512
-Thank you for the food.
-Let's eat.

208
00:10:09,447 --> 00:10:10,481
Yummy!

209
00:10:10,548 --> 00:10:12,349
It's delicious!

210
00:10:12,416 --> 00:10:13,951
Make sure you chew your food.

211
00:10:14,018 --> 00:10:16,654
Curry is not a drink, got it?

212
00:10:16,721 --> 00:10:18,055
Stop that.

213
00:10:18,122 --> 00:10:20,091
I understand you must be worried.

214
00:10:21,425 --> 00:10:22,460
Yes.

215
00:10:23,761 --> 00:10:28,766
I'm not really sure what's troubling her.

216
00:10:30,234 --> 00:10:32,369
Even when I ask, she won't tell me.

217
00:10:34,305 --> 00:10:38,909
Did anything change around the time
she started the second year?

218
00:10:38,976 --> 00:10:41,045
For example, were there any school events?

219
00:10:45,483 --> 00:10:47,618
You can draw whatever you want.

220
00:10:48,619 --> 00:10:49,587
All right.

221
00:10:50,354 --> 00:10:51,889
Okay.

222
00:10:58,562 --> 00:11:00,631
How about we play word chain art?

223
00:11:03,234 --> 00:11:04,468
I'll start.

224
00:11:06,470 --> 00:11:08,172
Let's see.

225
00:11:18,382 --> 00:11:19,216
Your turn.

226
00:11:34,398 --> 00:11:35,332
All right.

227
00:11:38,035 --> 00:11:39,937
Let's see what I can do.

228
00:11:43,274 --> 00:11:45,876
Maybe I'll add color to it.

229
00:11:56,086 --> 00:11:59,490
When you use your finger
to blend the color like this…

230
00:11:59,557 --> 00:12:01,058
It looks good, right?

231
00:12:02,793 --> 00:12:07,164
If we're going to use soft pastels…

232
00:12:11,402 --> 00:12:13,270
This drawing paper would be best.

233
00:12:14,071 --> 00:12:14,905
Here.

234
00:12:39,029 --> 00:12:41,532
Is that a sparrow?

235
00:12:50,507 --> 00:12:52,743
That looks good. Draw some more.

236
00:13:11,262 --> 00:13:13,230
That one is all alone.

237
00:13:17,334 --> 00:13:18,402
I guess so.

238
00:13:20,271 --> 00:13:21,171
I see.

239
00:13:29,647 --> 00:13:31,081
How does that sparrow feel?

240
00:13:49,934 --> 00:13:51,669
This area is empty. Can I draw here?

241
00:13:54,238 --> 00:13:55,406
You drew a sparrow,

242
00:13:55,906 --> 00:13:57,174
so I'll draw the next one.

243
00:13:57,241 --> 00:14:00,544
Let's see, I'll draw…

244
00:14:00,611 --> 00:14:01,645
I don't know.

245
00:14:26,670 --> 00:14:28,672
Let's continue this next time.

246
00:14:33,911 --> 00:14:38,649
NOT GOING TO SCHOOL
IS ALSO ONE WAY OF LIFE

247
00:14:38,716 --> 00:14:39,984
-Bye.
-Bye.

248
00:14:40,050 --> 00:14:41,618
-Bye.
-Be careful.

249
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:45,322
Sorry for causing you so much trouble.

250
00:14:45,389 --> 00:14:46,924
Not at all.

251
00:14:47,925 --> 00:14:50,027
Throwing that playdough
helped you blow off steam, right?

252
00:14:50,694 --> 00:14:51,862
Bye.

253
00:14:51,929 --> 00:14:55,165
It seems like he constantly
throws tantrums at school too.

254
00:14:56,700 --> 00:14:57,534
You can do it.

255
00:14:58,469 --> 00:15:01,672
-I did it!
-Yeah!

256
00:15:05,342 --> 00:15:06,443
Stop it!

257
00:15:08,345 --> 00:15:10,414
Whoa, let's get away from him!

258
00:15:10,481 --> 00:15:12,583
<i>I ask him why he'd do such a thing,</i>

259
00:15:13,183 --> 00:15:14,051
but to no avail.

260
00:15:14,118 --> 00:15:15,185
-Bye.
-Bye.

261
00:15:15,252 --> 00:15:16,086
Well,

262
00:15:16,754 --> 00:15:20,157
if you ever feel like really letting loose
and throwing something again,

263
00:15:20,824 --> 00:15:22,593
we've got Ms. Shizuku here.

264
00:15:22,659 --> 00:15:24,762
Hold on, I'm not a shooting target.

265
00:15:24,828 --> 00:15:27,264
-I'm really sorry.
-It's all right.

266
00:15:27,831 --> 00:15:28,999
We'll be going now.

267
00:15:29,066 --> 00:15:29,900
Bye.

268
00:15:34,805 --> 00:15:36,774
Ayaka. See you again.

269
00:15:44,848 --> 00:15:45,983
I'm back.

270
00:15:46,050 --> 00:15:48,285
Welcome home. How was it?

271
00:15:50,621 --> 00:15:51,455
I drew.

272
00:15:52,990 --> 00:15:53,824
That's good.

273
00:15:54,625 --> 00:15:56,293
I'm glad you had fun.

274
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:05,369
About school tomorrow…

275
00:16:08,739 --> 00:16:10,607
Never mind.

276
00:16:15,279 --> 00:16:16,847
Good work, everyone.

277
00:16:18,048 --> 00:16:19,450
-Hello, Professor.
-Hello.

278
00:16:19,516 --> 00:16:21,418
I started working here today.

279
00:16:21,485 --> 00:16:22,719
This is Shi-chan.

280
00:16:22,786 --> 00:16:23,887
-I'm Shi-chan.
-Shi-chan?

281
00:16:23,954 --> 00:16:25,222
-Nice to meet you.
-Likewise.

282
00:16:26,423 --> 00:16:27,624
This is for everyone.

283
00:16:28,692 --> 00:16:29,927
You were on a trip?

284
00:16:29,993 --> 00:16:32,229
It was an academic conference
for art therapy.

285
00:16:32,296 --> 00:16:33,197
Oh, right.

286
00:16:34,331 --> 00:16:35,466
What's art therapy?

287
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:38,001
I'm not entirely sure myself,

288
00:16:38,068 --> 00:16:40,971
but I guess it's something like
expressing your feelings

289
00:16:41,038 --> 00:16:43,907
and finding healing through art.

290
00:16:43,974 --> 00:16:45,976
Shi-chan, how was your first day?

291
00:16:46,043 --> 00:16:48,979
Well, it was one surprise after another.

292
00:16:49,046 --> 00:16:51,315
I realized everyone
is free to do whatever they want.

293
00:16:51,381 --> 00:16:53,383
Whether that's drawing or playing games.

294
00:16:53,450 --> 00:16:54,284
That's right.

295
00:16:54,351 --> 00:16:57,187
Yeah, our policy is to leave everything
up to the kids.

296
00:16:57,254 --> 00:16:59,957
They're free to play video games,
and free to do sports.

297
00:17:00,023 --> 00:17:01,291
-Right?
-Yeah.

298
00:17:01,358 --> 00:17:04,695
But Ayaka's mother, who visited today,

299
00:17:04,761 --> 00:17:07,064
was worried about her daughter's studies.

300
00:17:07,764 --> 00:17:08,899
Mr. Tatsuki told her

301
00:17:08,966 --> 00:17:11,869
that if she wants her to study,
she should throw away her textbooks.

302
00:17:13,237 --> 00:17:16,106
It's true that for some kids,
seeing textbooks lined up on the shelf

303
00:17:16,173 --> 00:17:17,708
can become a source of pressure.

304
00:17:19,309 --> 00:17:22,145
So, one approach is to remove the books
out of sight once

305
00:17:22,212 --> 00:17:24,748
and wait until they regain
the desire to study again.

306
00:17:24,815 --> 00:17:26,450
I see.

307
00:17:26,517 --> 00:17:27,951
That's why they need to be tossed.

308
00:17:28,552 --> 00:17:29,786
They shouldn't be tossed away.

309
00:17:30,420 --> 00:17:32,456
Ayaka was drawing today.

310
00:17:33,223 --> 00:17:35,726
Oh, she drew, huh?
I want to take a look at it.

311
00:17:35,792 --> 00:17:36,960
-This way.
-Let me see it.

312
00:17:37,628 --> 00:17:40,097
First we played word chain art,

313
00:17:40,964 --> 00:17:42,032
then she drew this.

314
00:17:45,469 --> 00:17:47,037
Did she mention anything about school?

315
00:17:48,172 --> 00:17:49,406
No, nothing.

316
00:17:49,973 --> 00:17:51,141
I see.

317
00:17:52,109 --> 00:17:52,976
Um…

318
00:17:55,279 --> 00:17:58,248
I heard from Ayaka's mother today…

319
00:17:59,016 --> 00:18:02,986
Did anything change around the time
she started the second year?

320
00:18:05,989 --> 00:18:08,959
There was a field trip.

321
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:11,695
Field trip, huh.

322
00:18:12,796 --> 00:18:15,699
Something might've happened
between her and her friends.

323
00:18:17,167 --> 00:18:19,303
Can I look into this a little?

324
00:18:19,369 --> 00:18:20,737
No need to do that.

325
00:18:20,804 --> 00:18:22,372
It's better to resolve this quickly.

326
00:18:23,140 --> 00:18:25,509
I know a few teachers
at Kita Middle School.

327
00:18:25,576 --> 00:18:28,378
I think she'll tell us the details
when she's ready to.

328
00:18:28,445 --> 00:18:30,247
Now, now.

329
00:18:30,314 --> 00:18:31,615
Just ask around casually.

330
00:18:32,282 --> 00:18:33,283
Okay.

331
00:18:39,456 --> 00:18:42,226
By the way, how's that kid
who throws tantrums?

332
00:18:42,759 --> 00:18:43,660
Yuuki?

333
00:18:44,561 --> 00:18:45,529
How's he doing?

334
00:18:48,565 --> 00:18:51,702
I allowed him
to really let loose today, but…

335
00:18:51,768 --> 00:18:53,003
-Get away!
-Ouch!

336
00:18:53,070 --> 00:18:53,971
Strike 'em down!

337
00:18:54,571 --> 00:18:57,708
I honestly don't know if that was
the right thing to do.

338
00:19:00,611 --> 00:19:02,646
Then the next step

339
00:19:02,713 --> 00:19:05,482
is to figure out how to help him
control those emotions.

340
00:19:06,316 --> 00:19:07,150
Control?

341
00:19:10,153 --> 00:19:12,022
Well, I'm off now.

342
00:19:12,089 --> 00:19:13,257
Bye.

343
00:19:20,397 --> 00:19:21,565
<i>Don't come in here!</i>

344
00:19:21,632 --> 00:19:22,899
Go away!

345
00:19:25,402 --> 00:19:26,503
Sora! Open up!

346
00:19:32,075 --> 00:19:34,811
MUSASHINO KITA MIDDLE SCHOOL

347
00:19:48,825 --> 00:19:49,693
Ms. Aomine,

348
00:19:49,760 --> 00:19:50,994
long time no see.

349
00:19:51,061 --> 00:19:52,562
Sorry to bother you like this.

350
00:19:52,629 --> 00:19:53,630
Not at all.

351
00:19:53,697 --> 00:19:57,367
We want to address the issue
of school refusal as soon as possible,

352
00:19:57,434 --> 00:20:00,537
-so this is actually a big help.
-Thank you.

353
00:20:01,104 --> 00:20:03,507
He was in the same group as her
during the field trip,

354
00:20:03,573 --> 00:20:05,876
and he seems to know a little
about the situation.

355
00:20:06,843 --> 00:20:08,378
Sorry to bother you during lunch.

356
00:20:08,879 --> 00:20:09,913
Not at all.

357
00:20:10,914 --> 00:20:14,184
Do you have any idea why Ayaka

358
00:20:14,251 --> 00:20:17,087
stopped coming to school?

359
00:20:18,555 --> 00:20:19,556
It's probably

360
00:20:21,224 --> 00:20:22,426
my fault.

361
00:20:32,402 --> 00:20:34,538
Hey, it's almost time to meet up
with everyone.

362
00:20:35,972 --> 00:20:36,873
You're not done yet?

363
00:20:40,977 --> 00:20:41,945
We'll be going now.

364
00:20:46,149 --> 00:20:47,150
Let's go.

365
00:20:47,984 --> 00:20:49,953
<i>I didn't say anything more</i>

366
00:20:50,020 --> 00:20:52,022
<i>and we left her there.</i>

367
00:20:56,693 --> 00:20:58,562
Thanks for telling me.

368
00:21:04,701 --> 00:21:05,669
That's so cool.

369
00:21:11,608 --> 00:21:12,576
-Damn it!
-Yuuki!

370
00:21:31,928 --> 00:21:32,963
Yuuki.

371
00:21:36,032 --> 00:21:38,468
This car is just like you.

372
00:21:40,904 --> 00:21:42,506
-What?
-Look.

373
00:21:43,807 --> 00:21:46,443
It has the ability to go super-fast!

374
00:21:49,312 --> 00:21:50,914
When it's angry,
it has strong attack power.

375
00:21:54,584 --> 00:21:55,652
That's like me?

376
00:22:01,191 --> 00:22:02,592
Try driving it yourself.

377
00:22:09,633 --> 00:22:11,968
Try driving it slowly.

378
00:22:14,404 --> 00:22:15,338
Vroom, vroom.

379
00:22:15,906 --> 00:22:17,607
-Vroom, vroom.
-Good.

380
00:22:17,674 --> 00:22:19,009
Make it go even slower.

381
00:22:19,743 --> 00:22:20,877
I want it to go faster.

382
00:22:22,112 --> 00:22:24,748
Then try gradually increasing the speed.

383
00:22:33,256 --> 00:22:34,925
-Vroom, vroom!
-That's good!

384
00:22:36,326 --> 00:22:38,728
Little by little. Good job.

385
00:22:40,764 --> 00:22:42,299
Yuuki. Stop.

386
00:22:42,365 --> 00:22:43,567
Stop!

387
00:22:45,702 --> 00:22:48,071
Good job, Yuuki. Excellent driver.

388
00:22:49,372 --> 00:22:50,674
Hey.

389
00:22:52,175 --> 00:22:55,879
If you ever reach a point
when you feel overwhelmed,

390
00:22:57,047 --> 00:22:58,081
think about this car.

391
00:23:06,823 --> 00:23:07,858
Mr. Tatsuki.

392
00:23:10,894 --> 00:23:13,463
So according to that group leader,
the source of the issue

393
00:23:13,530 --> 00:23:16,333
might be the fact that Ayaka
ended up getting left behind

394
00:23:16,399 --> 00:23:19,336
because she was so absorbed
with her drawing.

395
00:23:20,337 --> 00:23:21,171
And then?

396
00:23:22,606 --> 00:23:25,575
It seems he's going to apologize
to Ayaka in person today.

397
00:23:36,620 --> 00:23:39,823
We're very sorry.

398
00:23:39,890 --> 00:23:40,724
Not at all.

399
00:23:41,291 --> 00:23:43,560
Thank you for coming all the way here.

400
00:23:44,794 --> 00:23:45,829
See you at school.

401
00:23:47,864 --> 00:23:49,533
Thank you for your time today.

402
00:23:50,033 --> 00:23:51,268
Thank you.

403
00:23:55,939 --> 00:23:57,207
I see.

404
00:23:58,942 --> 00:24:00,110
So that's what happened?

405
00:24:04,080 --> 00:24:07,217
But it's nice that he came to apologize.

406
00:24:07,817 --> 00:24:08,785
Can you go to school?

407
00:24:10,220 --> 00:24:11,288
Yeah.

408
00:24:12,022 --> 00:24:12,856
Okay.

409
00:24:13,690 --> 00:24:16,526
I'm glad! I'm really glad.

410
00:24:21,398 --> 00:24:22,232
Good morning.

411
00:24:22,299 --> 00:24:23,733
Good morning.

412
00:24:23,800 --> 00:24:24,768
That's nice.

413
00:24:24,834 --> 00:24:26,403
-It's crazy, right?
-Yeah.

414
00:24:26,469 --> 00:24:28,638
So then what happened?

415
00:24:36,379 --> 00:24:37,681
Playing any games lately?

416
00:24:49,359 --> 00:24:51,227
First period we have music.

417
00:24:51,294 --> 00:24:52,629
-Oh, no.
-Oh, crap.

418
00:24:52,696 --> 00:24:53,964
I totally forgot.

419
00:24:54,030 --> 00:24:55,198
Let's hurry.

420
00:24:55,265 --> 00:24:56,099
Oh no.

421
00:24:56,166 --> 00:24:57,400
This is bad.

422
00:25:11,915 --> 00:25:12,749
<i>Ayaka</i>

423
00:25:12,816 --> 00:25:14,618
hasn't come back after that one time.

424
00:25:15,118 --> 00:25:16,987
It seems like she went to school today.

425
00:25:18,388 --> 00:25:20,123
I hope things are going well.

426
00:25:20,190 --> 00:25:21,291
Yeah.

427
00:25:22,826 --> 00:25:25,528
I've experienced school refusal myself,
but the longer it drags on,

428
00:25:25,595 --> 00:25:27,397
the harder it gets to go back.

429
00:25:29,699 --> 00:25:30,767
Is that right?

430
00:25:32,002 --> 00:25:34,237
That's why I can kind of understand

431
00:25:34,304 --> 00:25:36,306
Ayaka's feelings.

432
00:25:43,813 --> 00:25:44,848
Hello, it's Yukanai.

433
00:25:45,749 --> 00:25:47,684
Is Ayaka there?

434
00:25:48,551 --> 00:25:50,420
No, she's not here.

435
00:25:51,554 --> 00:25:53,790
I just got a call from her school.

436
00:25:53,857 --> 00:25:55,925
It seems she left school
without telling anyone.

437
00:25:58,328 --> 00:25:59,529
I'll search for her too.

438
00:26:30,160 --> 00:26:32,929
Shall we continue drawing
where we left off?

439
00:26:34,330 --> 00:26:35,231
‎What?

440
00:26:41,571 --> 00:26:42,472
Here.

441
00:26:46,643 --> 00:26:47,877
With pastels,

442
00:26:48,511 --> 00:26:50,580
you can erase them if you want,

443
00:26:50,647 --> 00:26:51,981
or you can layer them.

444
00:26:52,615 --> 00:26:53,817
You're free to do whatever.

445
00:26:57,520 --> 00:27:00,590
I wonder why she left school early.

446
00:27:02,158 --> 00:27:02,992
Yeah, I wonder.

447
00:27:21,010 --> 00:27:23,213
Do you like to draw?

448
00:27:26,783 --> 00:27:29,352
When I was in college,
I spent all my time drawing.

449
00:27:30,186 --> 00:27:32,188
Can you draw too, Teacher?

450
00:27:33,156 --> 00:27:34,157
Call me Tatsuki.

451
00:27:34,991 --> 00:27:36,426
Tatsuki, draw with me.

452
00:28:09,259 --> 00:28:10,093
What's that?

453
00:28:11,461 --> 00:28:12,295
It's a birdcage.

454
00:28:16,232 --> 00:28:19,469
Those birds are in the birdcage?

455
00:28:21,337 --> 00:28:22,472
Then

456
00:28:23,640 --> 00:28:24,774
is that other bird

457
00:28:25,408 --> 00:28:27,477
planning to fly off somewhere?

458
00:28:37,120 --> 00:28:38,454
I don't know.

459
00:28:41,591 --> 00:28:42,458
I see.

460
00:28:58,241 --> 00:29:00,777
Ayaka's mother contacted us.

461
00:29:01,444 --> 00:29:03,680
She said Ayaka just got back home.

462
00:29:07,817 --> 00:29:10,220
Did you understand anything
from her drawings?

463
00:29:12,989 --> 00:29:14,090
Nope.

464
00:29:15,158 --> 00:29:17,393
I don't know what Ayaka is going through.

465
00:29:18,928 --> 00:29:20,797
Is it still difficult

466
00:29:21,364 --> 00:29:22,632
even with art therapy?

467
00:29:25,802 --> 00:29:28,037
It doesn't always give us direct answers.

468
00:29:31,574 --> 00:29:35,078
Could it be
that this birdcage and the sparrows

469
00:29:35,144 --> 00:29:37,647
represent her school and friends?

470
00:29:38,615 --> 00:29:40,216
From Ayaka's perspective

471
00:29:40,717 --> 00:29:44,387
maybe there's this insurmountable wall
keeping her from going to school.

472
00:29:45,355 --> 00:29:46,656
She doesn't need to go.

473
00:29:49,826 --> 00:29:52,161
You don't have to force yourself
to go to school.

474
00:29:52,662 --> 00:29:53,663
Those who want to should go.

475
00:29:54,264 --> 00:29:56,299
That's not how it works.

476
00:29:58,668 --> 00:30:01,838
Ms. Shizuku, you sound just like
a schoolteacher.

477
00:30:01,905 --> 00:30:04,574
Couldn't you be a little more flexible
in your thinking?

478
00:30:04,641 --> 00:30:05,541
No.

479
00:30:06,342 --> 00:30:08,578
Just imagine how worried parents get

480
00:30:08,645 --> 00:30:10,213
when their child won't go to school.

481
00:30:12,849 --> 00:30:15,551
I'm sure deep down Ayaka knows this too.

482
00:30:16,452 --> 00:30:18,321
She wants to go but she can't.

483
00:30:19,589 --> 00:30:21,224
But if she continues to stay home,

484
00:30:22,091 --> 00:30:24,060
she knows she'll never
be able to go at all.

485
00:30:25,161 --> 00:30:25,995
That's why

486
00:30:26,796 --> 00:30:28,564
she makes the effort to go.

487
00:30:28,631 --> 00:30:30,133
No one needs to force themselves to go.

488
00:30:30,700 --> 00:30:31,901
What?

489
00:30:33,536 --> 00:30:36,105
I'm going to step out.
Take care of things here.

490
00:30:44,747 --> 00:30:45,581
He's so annoying!

491
00:30:46,983 --> 00:30:49,919
Shi-chan, eat slowly.

492
00:30:49,986 --> 00:30:51,487
What's wrong with that guy?

493
00:30:51,554 --> 00:30:54,057
He's got a super naive mindset,
but is he all right?

494
00:30:55,224 --> 00:30:57,126
I totally understand. It's worrisome, huh?

495
00:30:59,295 --> 00:31:00,897
I understand that this place

496
00:31:00,964 --> 00:31:03,766
is necessary
for children who have been hurt.

497
00:31:03,833 --> 00:31:05,635
But it's only natural for parents

498
00:31:05,702 --> 00:31:07,603
to be worried about their children's

499
00:31:07,670 --> 00:31:08,972
studies and their future.

500
00:31:09,038 --> 00:31:10,606
You're right.

501
00:31:10,673 --> 00:31:14,143
And yet he says kids should be free
and not be forced to go to school.

502
00:31:14,210 --> 00:31:16,279
Isn't that just completely irresponsible?

503
00:31:16,346 --> 00:31:19,182
I understand,
but that's too much hot sauce.

504
00:31:21,184 --> 00:31:22,151
Sorry.

505
00:31:22,218 --> 00:31:25,555
Personally, I think it's great to have
different perspectives.

506
00:31:25,621 --> 00:31:27,223
Given your background as a teacher,

507
00:31:27,290 --> 00:31:29,359
you're able to empathize
with parents' feelings.

508
00:31:29,425 --> 00:31:31,561
That's necessary here too.

509
00:31:32,195 --> 00:31:33,830
Thank you.

510
00:31:34,430 --> 00:31:37,734
Well, it seems like he has his own way
of dealing with things.

511
00:31:37,800 --> 00:31:38,935
Or so I think.

512
00:31:41,771 --> 00:31:43,106
He's so annoying!

513
00:31:48,678 --> 00:31:50,246
I thought the problem was solved.

514
00:31:50,813 --> 00:31:52,315
The other kid apologized, right?

515
00:31:53,349 --> 00:31:55,418
But she left school early, so I think

516
00:31:55,485 --> 00:31:56,919
there's something else going on.

517
00:31:56,986 --> 00:31:58,221
Like what?

518
00:31:59,155 --> 00:32:00,957
What did Ayaka say?

519
00:32:01,991 --> 00:32:05,395
I've asked her, but she won't tell me.

520
00:32:06,162 --> 00:32:07,797
But even so,

521
00:32:07,864 --> 00:32:09,532
we can't just leave this problem alone.

522
00:32:10,233 --> 00:32:12,268
And what if she falls behind
in her studies?

523
00:32:13,336 --> 00:32:15,371
She's the one who'll struggle
in the future.

524
00:32:16,706 --> 00:32:19,876
It's best to solve this
as soon as possible.

525
00:32:19,942 --> 00:32:20,777
Yeah.

526
00:32:30,486 --> 00:32:31,554
I'll be off.

527
00:32:32,588 --> 00:32:33,423
Bye.

528
00:33:11,794 --> 00:33:13,196
-Wait up.
-Okay.

529
00:33:13,262 --> 00:33:15,498
-You can't run into the street.
-I can do a new trick.

530
00:33:15,565 --> 00:33:17,600
-Just watch.
-Go play over there.

531
00:33:17,667 --> 00:33:18,568
Okay.

532
00:33:20,403 --> 00:33:22,004
Oh.

533
00:33:22,071 --> 00:33:23,005
Ayaka.

534
00:33:28,044 --> 00:33:29,145
Ta-da!

535
00:33:29,212 --> 00:33:32,315
A 242-color set of soft pastels!

536
00:33:32,849 --> 00:33:35,051
There were so many colors
I had run out of.

537
00:33:35,118 --> 00:33:36,219
So I decided to splurge.

538
00:33:37,220 --> 00:33:38,287
I see.

539
00:33:38,354 --> 00:33:39,222
Look at this.

540
00:33:39,288 --> 00:33:42,291
The gradation from green to blue
is so cool, isn't it?

541
00:33:43,926 --> 00:33:44,961
Yeah, it's cool.

542
00:33:47,463 --> 00:33:48,297
Here.

543
00:33:49,432 --> 00:33:50,266
Go ahead.

544
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:51,901
Feel free to use it.

545
00:34:35,545 --> 00:34:37,146
It's raining?

546
00:34:45,955 --> 00:34:47,557
That sparrow will get wet.

547
00:34:48,424 --> 00:34:49,458
What's it going to do?

548
00:35:08,344 --> 00:35:09,612
Tatsuki.

549
00:35:19,021 --> 00:35:20,189
Tatsuki.

550
00:35:26,829 --> 00:35:27,964
I don't

551
00:35:29,065 --> 00:35:30,099
want to go to school.

552
00:35:35,705 --> 00:35:36,639
I see.

553
00:35:40,710 --> 00:35:42,578
You were able to express your feelings.

554
00:35:52,388 --> 00:35:53,356
If

555
00:35:54,423 --> 00:35:56,359
you have something you want to say,

556
00:35:58,060 --> 00:35:59,895
don't keep it bottled up inside.

557
00:36:00,796 --> 00:36:02,765
You can talk about anything you like here.

558
00:36:06,235 --> 00:36:07,203
Okay,

559
00:36:09,872 --> 00:36:11,374
you don't want to go to school, huh.

560
00:36:14,844 --> 00:36:18,047
I've always been scared
of being in the classroom.

561
00:36:22,618 --> 00:36:23,686
But

562
00:36:27,023 --> 00:36:28,557
I couldn't tell anyone about it.

563
00:36:30,893 --> 00:36:32,161
I see.

564
00:36:33,396 --> 00:36:34,830
That's understandable.

565
00:36:37,967 --> 00:36:38,968
And…

566
00:36:42,605 --> 00:36:44,407
I can't tell Mom about this.

567
00:36:50,212 --> 00:36:51,047
Okay.

568
00:36:53,182 --> 00:36:55,184
I see.

569
00:36:55,251 --> 00:36:57,420
I suppose the stifling pressure

570
00:36:57,486 --> 00:37:00,823
of school life just gradually built up
over time.

571
00:37:02,958 --> 00:37:06,028
But it's amazing that she was able
to voice that herself.

572
00:37:06,529 --> 00:37:09,532
But she said she can't bring herself
to tell her mom yet.

573
00:37:11,267 --> 00:37:13,903
It must be tough
when you can't reach out for help

574
00:37:13,969 --> 00:37:15,404
-to the person closest to you.
-Yes.

575
00:37:19,575 --> 00:37:21,477
I don't know how to help her.

576
00:37:23,746 --> 00:37:27,383
To truly understand Ayaka's feelings,

577
00:37:27,917 --> 00:37:29,752
you might need to take a deeper look

578
00:37:30,319 --> 00:37:32,655
at whatever she focuses on

579
00:37:32,722 --> 00:37:34,790
and pours her energy into.

580
00:37:42,598 --> 00:37:44,567
I thought you hated schools.

581
00:37:44,633 --> 00:37:46,202
I never said that.

582
00:37:46,268 --> 00:37:48,738
You were totally against it.

583
00:37:48,804 --> 00:37:51,841
I only got permission on the condition
that we stay in the hallway,

584
00:37:51,907 --> 00:37:53,676
so please don't go into the classroom…

585
00:37:53,743 --> 00:37:55,378
Hey, weren't you listening?

586
00:37:56,379 --> 00:37:59,115
I want to look at the artwork
she drew at the zoo.

587
00:37:59,181 --> 00:38:00,616
Oh, come on.

588
00:38:03,419 --> 00:38:04,420
Hey.

589
00:38:05,187 --> 00:38:08,691
MEMORIES FROM THE FIELD TRIP

590
00:38:08,758 --> 00:38:09,992
There it is.

591
00:38:13,295 --> 00:38:15,398
AYAKA SAOTOME
CLASS 2-2

592
00:38:28,611 --> 00:38:29,445
Ms. Shizuku.

593
00:38:30,012 --> 00:38:30,846
Yes?

594
00:38:32,348 --> 00:38:33,282
Let's take this drawing.

595
00:38:34,049 --> 00:38:35,851
No, you can't do that!

596
00:38:35,918 --> 00:38:36,852
-What?
-You can't!

597
00:38:38,854 --> 00:38:39,688
This is

598
00:38:40,456 --> 00:38:42,291
what Ayaka drew when she was here.

599
00:38:44,093 --> 00:38:47,463
It seems very lonely.

600
00:38:49,665 --> 00:38:50,933
You're referring to this bird?

601
00:38:52,201 --> 00:38:54,003
It looks lonely

602
00:38:55,104 --> 00:38:56,672
being away from its friends.

603
00:38:57,540 --> 00:38:59,875
I thought so too at first.

604
00:39:02,478 --> 00:39:03,646
I thought this was the school,

605
00:39:04,613 --> 00:39:07,049
and while everyone inside is having fun,

606
00:39:07,116 --> 00:39:10,052
she couldn't break down the thick wall
to join everyone.

607
00:39:11,053 --> 00:39:11,954
Yes.

608
00:39:12,021 --> 00:39:12,888
But

609
00:39:13,656 --> 00:39:15,691
I don't think these are her friends,

610
00:39:17,660 --> 00:39:19,061
but her family instead.

611
00:39:22,198 --> 00:39:23,466
What do you mean?

612
00:39:24,867 --> 00:39:27,436
The birdcage isn't a wall
standing in her way,

613
00:39:27,503 --> 00:39:30,873
but rather a barrier
that's protecting her.

614
00:39:32,775 --> 00:39:35,778
Therefore, I don't think this represents
the school,

615
00:39:36,846 --> 00:39:38,781
but her home instead.

616
00:39:40,683 --> 00:39:42,852
Are you saying
that she wants to stay home?

617
00:39:44,453 --> 00:39:47,189
Is there anything that comes to mind?

618
00:39:50,459 --> 00:39:51,360
Well,

619
00:39:52,194 --> 00:39:56,232
Ayaka has always said
that she wants to go to school.

620
00:39:57,233 --> 00:39:58,400
But she told me

621
00:39:59,568 --> 00:40:01,437
that she doesn't want to go to school.

622
00:40:02,271 --> 00:40:03,105
What?

623
00:40:03,172 --> 00:40:05,374
She said she can't bring herself
to tell you about it.

624
00:40:08,811 --> 00:40:09,912
But why?

625
00:40:11,347 --> 00:40:13,582
I didn't understand either, but…

626
00:40:23,726 --> 00:40:25,261
Please take a look at this.

627
00:40:26,529 --> 00:40:30,833
This is what Ayaka drew at the zoo.

628
00:40:31,433 --> 00:40:32,935
When I look at this,

629
00:40:34,136 --> 00:40:35,337
I get the sense

630
00:40:36,372 --> 00:40:38,407
that this parent and child
share a deep bond

631
00:40:39,241 --> 00:40:43,579
and place a great deal of trust
in one another.

632
00:40:46,649 --> 00:40:48,017
That's how it seems

633
00:40:49,084 --> 00:40:51,287
to me too.

634
00:40:55,190 --> 00:40:56,659
I think Ayaka

635
00:40:58,093 --> 00:41:00,296
couldn't bring herself
to express her true feelings

636
00:41:01,363 --> 00:41:04,033
because her mother is so important to her.

637
00:41:27,890 --> 00:41:28,924
Ayaka.

638
00:41:32,294 --> 00:41:33,262
This

639
00:41:34,129 --> 00:41:35,397
is a beautiful drawing.

640
00:41:44,139 --> 00:41:45,741
The truth is,

641
00:41:46,976 --> 00:41:49,445
I never wanted to go to school.

642
00:42:05,327 --> 00:42:09,031
I'm sorry I never told you the truth.

643
00:42:17,006 --> 00:42:18,007
It's all right.

644
00:42:20,242 --> 00:42:21,510
I was always

645
00:42:22,745 --> 00:42:25,581
a little too relieved whenever

646
00:42:26,281 --> 00:42:27,883
you went to school, huh?

647
00:42:31,120 --> 00:42:33,789
That's why you couldn't
tell me the truth, right?

648
00:42:37,459 --> 00:42:38,627
I'm sorry.

649
00:43:06,855 --> 00:43:09,458
Time to counterattack!

650
00:43:09,525 --> 00:43:10,659
Stop!

651
00:43:12,194 --> 00:43:13,929
Hooray!

652
00:43:22,671 --> 00:43:24,440
<i>When you feel overwhelmed,</i>

653
00:43:25,841 --> 00:43:27,409
think about this car.

654
00:43:40,856 --> 00:43:41,690
Time to escape!

655
00:43:41,757 --> 00:43:43,992
-No way.
-Hold on.

656
00:43:48,931 --> 00:43:50,599
You're going to Yukanai today, right?

657
00:43:51,500 --> 00:43:52,468
Here's your lunch.

658
00:43:52,968 --> 00:43:55,604
I put in your favorite Hamburg steak
to cheer you up!

659
00:43:59,274 --> 00:44:00,375
Thank you.

660
00:44:01,076 --> 00:44:03,479
But right now, my favorite food
is <i>kinpira gobo</i>.

661
00:44:03,545 --> 00:44:04,747
It is?

662
00:44:04,813 --> 00:44:06,181
Since when?

663
00:44:06,682 --> 00:44:09,351
Children grow up before you know it.

664
00:44:09,852 --> 00:44:11,620
Oh, is that right?

665
00:44:12,387 --> 00:44:14,723
Then I'll add that to your lunch
next time.

666
00:44:16,992 --> 00:44:18,093
Thank you.

667
00:44:18,794 --> 00:44:19,628
I'll be off.

668
00:44:20,496 --> 00:44:21,330
Have fun.

669
00:44:55,631 --> 00:44:56,498
Hello?

670
00:44:56,565 --> 00:44:58,901
Tatsuki. Sora… Sora…

671
00:45:00,102 --> 00:45:01,203
What happened to Sora?

672
00:45:01,270 --> 00:45:03,005
He jumped.

673
00:45:04,339 --> 00:45:05,174
What?

674
00:45:07,075 --> 00:45:08,944
PREVIEW OF THE NEXT EPISODE

675
00:45:09,011 --> 00:45:11,013
‎THIS DRAMA IS FICTION

676
00:45:11,079 --> 00:45:12,047
Subtitle translation by: Lili Morita

